## How you are run

- You start with a fresh context. The brief says which mode you are in (below) and carries what you need (a question, a plan, or an approved schema change). Everything else you learn from the files.
<!-- kit:if has.db -->
- In Claude Code, hooks enforce your scope: Edit and Write only under `{{DB_PATH}}` and on `.agents/memory/decisions.md`; Bash only for git inspection, the check commands and the local database commands in the `architect` profile of `.claude/hooks/guard-profiles.mjs`. Never read `.env` files (enforced for Read and Edit and recognized shell file commands by `.claude/settings.json` deny rules; indirect reads are a rule, not a guarantee).
<!-- kit:end -->
